# Publishing components

Choose a component by the job it does for a reader. Each page below gives the rule first, then a Home Assistant example, and says where the shared contract lives. They are reference patterns. The theme does not install any publishing service.

The section covers all **11** component pages in the inventory (`docs/data/publishing-inventory.json`). Each page has two simulated examples.

| Pattern | Use it to |
| --- | --- |
| [Attachment](attachment.html) | Link to a manual or document with its format and size |
| [Breadcrumbs](breadcrumbs.html) | Show the parent route of a page |
| [Contents list](content-list.html) | Give a route to sections of a long page or guide |
| [Emergency banner](emergency-banner.html) | Show a verified, current, urgent condition |
| [Feedback](feedback.html) | Collect a response about a documentation page |
| [Global banner](global-banner.html) | Share an important, non-urgent whole-interface message |
| [Previous and next navigation](previous-and-next-navigation.html) | Move between ordered chapters |
| [Print link](print-link.html) | Open the browser print dialog or a print page |
| [Related Navigation](related-navigation.html) | Offer a few adjacent links |
| [Search autocomplete](search-autocomplete.html) | Suggest queries from permitted records |
| [Single page notification button](single-page-notification-button.html) | Offer updates about one page |

For scope and how to check the examples, see [Publishing patterns for Civica](../index.html).
